WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:10.000
Relay turns a successful UI workflow into a reusable capability.
A model discovers the procedure. A deterministic engine runs it again.

00:10.000 --> 00:25.000
Discovery uses a real local language model.
It sees the current screen and chooses one permitted action at a time.

00:25.000 --> 00:43.000
The model searches for the member, opens the account, and reads the balance.
The executor verifies the final screen and the member identity.

00:43.000 --> 00:56.000
The result becomes a typed, versioned artifact.
Inputs, outputs, targets, actions and checkpoints are reviewable.

00:56.000 --> 01:09.000
Replay uses the same artifact with a different member.
The balance is extracted from the live UI, with no model decisions.

01:09.000 --> 01:19.000
A missing member returns a known business outcome.
It is useful information, not an automation crash.

01:19.000 --> 01:30.000
An expired session pauses automation and requests intervention.
The human receives control of the existing live session.

01:30.000 --> 01:40.000
Restore the session, then return control.
Automation resumes and verifies the original checkpoint.

01:40.000 --> 01:51.000
The same capability runs against a second institution's variant,
using an explicit control-name override.

01:51.000 --> 02:00.000
Every run produces redacted, inspectable evidence.
Discover once. Replay with control.
